<!-- ================= 1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY ================= -->
<h1>1. Executive Summary &amp; System Overview</h1>
<p>
  <strong>FlashCart</strong> is an enterprise-grade, high-concurrency eCommerce web application engineered specifically to solve the classical computational and concurrency bottlenecks encountered during <em>flash sales</em> and high-demand product drops.
</p>
<p>
  During high-traffic flash sale events, traditional eCommerce platforms frequently fail due to <strong>race conditions, inventory overselling, and database deadlocks</strong>. FlashCart incorporates strict atomic stock verification, isolated client-side cart states, and seamless warehouse operations into a unified, responsive platform.
</p>
<div class="callout">
  <div class="callout-title">Core Project Objectives</div>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Zero Oversell Guarantee:</strong> Guarantee that customer order quantities never exceed physically available warehouse stock, regardless of concurrent checkout attempts.</li>
    <li><strong>End-to-End Inventory Lifecycle Tracking:</strong> Track goods from warehouse intake to manufacturing date, real-time stock levels, and expiration monitoring.</li>
    <li><strong>Automated Perishable Alerts:</strong> Categorize products into expired (&lt; Today) and upcoming expiration (&le; 7 days) buckets with high-visibility color-coded badges.</li>
    <li><strong>Role-Based Administrative Security:</strong> Isolate warehouse management tools behind strict role-based access control (RBAC), multi-layered JWT session verification, and administrative provisioning wizards.</li>
    <li><strong>Seamless Direct Checkout:</strong> Frictionless, 1-click checkout simulation coupled with delivery pincode capture and an automated, printable receipt/tax invoice generator.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<!-- ================= 2. SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE & TECH STACK ================= -->
<h1>2. System Architecture &amp; Technology Stack</h1>
<p>
  The system follows a modern decoupled Cloud Architecture with Next.js App Router providing both the presentation layer (Server &amp; Client Components) and the serverless API micro-services.
</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Layer / Tier</th>
      <th>Technology / Tool</th>
      <th>Key Version</th>
      <th>Function &amp; Architectural Responsibility</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Frontend Framework</strong></td>
      <td>Next.js (App Router)</td>
      <td>15.x</td>
      <td>Server-Side Rendering (SSR), Static Generation, React Server Components &amp; Client State.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>UI Library</strong></td>
      <td>React</td>
      <td>19.x</td>
      <td>Declarative component-driven interfaces, reactive state hooks (<code>useState</code>, <code>useEffect</code>).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Styling &amp; Design</strong></td>
      <td>Tailwind CSS</td>
      <td>v4.0</td>
      <td>Utility-first CSS styling, mobile-first responsive design, modern CSS color palettes.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Authentication</strong></td>
      <td>Supabase Auth (GoTrue)</td>
      <td>v2</td>
      <td>JWT-based authentication, user metadata management, and encrypted session storage.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Backend API</strong></td>
      <td>Next.js Route Handlers</td>
      <td>15.x</td>
      <td>Serverless micro-endpoints for atomic stock verification, checkout, and admin tools.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Deployment &amp; Hosting</strong></td>
      <td>Vercel Edge Network</td>
      <td>Production</td>
      <td>Serverless function runtime, global CDN distribution, continuous integration &amp; deployment (CI/CD).</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- ================= 3. COMPLETE PAGE SPECIFICATIONS ================= -->
<h1>3. Frontend Architecture &amp; Complete Page Specifications</h1>
<p>
  FlashCart consists of 6 dedicated application pages and key modal flows. Every page is styled with Tailwind CSS v4, displays dynamic tab headers, and includes the institutional attribution footer.
</p>

<!-- 3.1 STOREFRONT -->
<h2>3.1 Customer Storefront &amp; Live Catalog Grid (<code>/</code> &bull; <code>app/page.tsx</code>)</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Target User:</strong> Retail shoppers and flash sale buyers.</li>
  <li><strong>Page Title:</strong> <code>FlashCart | Live Flash Sale Store</code></li>
  <li><strong>Key Features:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Flash Sale Hero Banner:</strong> Features live event metrics and countdown branding.</li>
      <li><strong>Catalog Search &amp; Filter:</strong> Instant dynamic search bar filtering by name or category, with fast category chips (<code>All</code>, <code>Electronics</code>, <code>Food</code>, etc.).</li>
      <li><strong>Stock Badge System:</strong> High-visibility badges indicating remaining inventory (e.g. <code>50 units left</code> in green, <code>3 units left</code> in bold red alert).</li>
      <li><strong>Flash Sale Oversell Guard in UI:</strong> Quantity stepper disables incrementing beyond remaining warehouse stock.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>

